1 NAME Abraham /ben Marchiv/
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1928
1 OCCU writer, merchant
1 NOTE Moved from Shechem (Nablus) to Jaffa: failed 1894 and 1902,
2 CONT succeeded 1905. Eight children. The move broke the community's
2 CONT isolation in Nablus and the settlement he founded now holds half
2 CONT the nation. A prominent literary figure of the household in the
2 CONT 19th century. Died 1928; his sons moved to Tel Aviv, then Holon
2 CONT in 1951.
2 CONT Sources: 'The Tsedaka Family', theSamaritanUpdate.com, 2008; Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page
