1 NAME Benyamim //
1 SEX M
1 OCCU shopkeeper
1 NOTE Father of Ratson. Kept a materials shop in Nablus market; an eye
2 CONT illness ended his work, which forced Ratson out of school to help.
2 CONT Source: 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMS @F136@
1 FAMC @F135@
0 @I153@ INDI
1 NAME Ratson /ben Benyamim/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 FEB 1922
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 JAN 1990
1 OCCU writer, poet, reader of the Law, singer
1 NOTE Born Nablus. Read the entire Torah at six; sang his first poem
2 CONT before the worshippers at eight. Married Batia bat Yefet in 1943.
2 CONT Moved to Tel Aviv 1951 under the Israel-Jordan family unification
2 CONT agreement, then Holon 1955. Ran a camping-equipment business from
2 CONT the early 1970s. Prof. Zeev Ben-Hayyim called him 'my teacher and
2 CONT mentor' and 'the sea of knowledge and traditions of the Samaritan
2 CONT Community'; Prof. Dov Noy called him the reviver of the Samaritan
2 CONT cultural renaissance. Recorded 400 hours of Samaritan tradition.
2 CONT Died on Shabbat, 20 January 1990.
2 CONT Source: 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMS @F137@
1 FAMC @F136@
0 @I154@ INDI
1 NAME Benyamim /ben Ratson/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1944
1 OCCU historian, editor
1 NOTE Born Nablus 1944. With his brother Yefet founded the bi-weekly
2 CONT A.B. - The Samaritan News in December 1969, and has been its chief
2 CONT editor since. Opened the A.B. Institute of Samaritan Studies at his
2 CONT home in Holon in 1981. Author of the sources this file is built
2 CONT from.
2 CONT Sources: Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page; 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMC @F137@
0 @I155@ INDI
1 NAME Yefet /ben Ratson/
1 SEX M
1 OCCU editor
1 NOTE With his brother Benyamim founded A.B. - The Samaritan News in
2 CONT December 1969.
2 CONT Source: 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMC @F137@
0 @I156@ INDI
1 NAME Gamliel //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Named through his son's patronymic.
2 CONT Source: Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page
1 FAMS @F138@
0 @I157@ INDI
1 NAME Yisrael /ben Gamliel/
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1932
1 OCCU sage, printer of Samaritan texts
1 NOTE Born 1932. Worked at the Israeli Society for the Production of
2 CONT Coins and Medals. Published Samaritan texts, prayer books and a
2 CONT detailed edition of the Samaritan Pentateuch; long association with
2 CONT Prof. Zeev Ben-Hayyim and Prof. Abraham Tal. With Ratson and
2 CONT Abraham ben Marchiv Hamarchivi printed copied manuscripts for
2 CONT community use.
2 CONT HAS FOUR SONS, ALL OF WHOM MARRIED JEWISH WOMEN WHO JOINED THE
2 CONT COMMUNITY - his own words to Sean Ireton. None of the four sons
2 CONT and none of the four wives is named in any source found. Those
2 CONT eight people are the most promising route from this genealogy to
2 CONT the wider world tree.
2 CONT Note also: Ireton calls him a Cohen (priestly), while the
2 CONT Institute places him in Tsedaka Hassafari, tribe of Menasseh.
2 CONT Unresolved.
2 CONT Sources: Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page; Sean Ireton, 'The Samaritans - A Jewish Sect in Israel'
1 FAMC @F138@
0 @I158@ INDI
1 NAME Nor //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Named through his son's patronymic.
2 CONT Source: 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMS @F139@
0 @I159@ INDI
1 NAME Abraham /ben Nor/
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Cousin of Ratson. Together they published the first comparative
2 CONT edition of the Jewish and Samaritan versions of the Torah,
2 CONT 1962-1965.
2 CONT Source: 'Ratson b. Benyamim Tsedaka - 90 Years to His Birthday', Benyamim Tsedaka, 2012
1 FAMC @F139@
0 @I160@ INDI
1 NAME Arieh Nimr Yisaschar /ben Shalma/
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Also given as Yisaschar. A cousin of Abraham ben Marchiv's father.
2 CONT Moved to Tul Karm, where his family lived nearly two generations
2 CONT without taking root. His branch, Dar Elnimir, ended when its last
2 CONT member died on 25 March 2012.
2 CONT Sources: 'The Tsedaka Family', theSamaritanUpdate.com, 2008; Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page
0 @I161@ INDI
1 NAME Ab-Sikuwwa //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Named through his sons' patronymics.
2 CONT Source: Israelite Samaritan Information Institute, families page
